{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Verification evidence (Phase 2 — landed as Gerrit 2360 patchset 7, MERGED to origin/main)\n\nRecording AC/DD completion evidence here (kept out of the description to stay under the plan-review admission cap).\n\n**Implementation (two seams):**\n- AC1/AC2 (mint-time warning): `_warn_if_verify_cannot_resolve` (+ `_ssh_pub_body`) in `mint_opcert_record` (`src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`) — logs a WARNING naming key_path + principal when the specific signed key's public counterpart is not in the same-environment verify resolver's set; still returns the signature.\n- AC3 (serve-degraded, never abort): `opcert_signing_status` / `opcert_signer_degraded` / `run_startup_opcert_check` (`src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py`), surfaced via `_mcp_health.py` `/health` `opcert` field + boot warning + `run_mcp` wiring. `expected` gates strictness like `store_status` (only when trusted-environment pinning is configured). Did NOT extend `compose_startup_opcert_binding` to abort; did NOT add a redundant derive probe.\n- AC4: both guards are in-process/operation-linked (mint path + server startup); no CI-provider dependency.\n\n**RED→GREEN + mutation proof:**\n- Held-out `tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py` (12 tests) covers DD1 (AC1/AC2 incl. the specific-key case where a different chain key's pub resolves yet the signed key's own counterpart is absent) and DD2 (AC3 degraded/matched/unbound/not-pinned). Asserts observable log/dict output with no CI env set (DD3/AC4).\n- Sandboxed mutation check: neuter the mint guard → 2 RED (AC1/AC2); force `opcert_signer_degraded`→False → 3 RED (AC3); restore → 12 GREEN.\n\n**CI / merge:** Gerrit Verified gate run 33265621222 — all pytest legs (ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13, macos py3.13) + lint/typecheck/mutation/optionality GREEN → Verified +1; LLM-Review +1 (2 advisory, non-blocking). Change 2360 SUBMITTED → MERGED.\n\n**Module-size compliance:** the rebase onto a grown origin/main tipped `_mcp_health.py` (877) and `_opcert_signing.py` (813) over the 800-LOC cap; resolved by extracting `_mcp_opcert_health.py` (115 LOC) and `_opcert_verify.py` (340 LOC) along existing call-graph seams (mint/verify + health/opcert). `verify_opcert_record` re-exported from `_opcert_signing` (lazy back-imports → no cycle; both import orders verified). All `src/rebar/*.py` ≤ 800; complexity baseline new=0/increased=0; `make lint` clean. file_impact widened to the 5 touched paths (re-running plan-review to re-certify the widened material)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788026567951139951,"uuid":"ed7c71f1-0b6c-48f2-a57b-90f916dcc467"}